## 🎮 Variable 1: HEADED - Browser Visibility

```bash
npm run test:headed          ← Browser opens (debug mode)
npm test                     ← Browser hidden (fast mode)
```

| Value | Behavior |
|-------|----------|
| `HEADED=true` | 👁️ Browser visible |
| `HEADED=false` | 🚫 Browser hidden (default) |

---

## 🏷️ Variable 2: CUCUMBER_TAGS - Test Filtering

```bash
npm run test:tags            ← Runs @smoke tests
CUCUMBER_TAGS="@regression" npm test   ← Runs @regression
CUCUMBER_TAGS="@critical and @smoke" npm test  ← Both required
CUCUMBER_TAGS="not @wip" npm test     ← Exclude @wip
```

**Syntax Examples:**
```
@tag                    → Single tag
@tag1 and @tag2        → Multiple (AND)
@tag1 or @tag2         → Multiple (OR)
not @tag               → Exclude
(@tag1 or @tag2) and not @tag3  → Complex
```

---

## ⚡ Variable 3: CUCUMBER_WORKERS - Parallel Execution

```bash
npm test                     ← Serial (one test at a time)
npm run test:parallel        ← 4 workers (parallel)
CUCUMBER_WORKERS=2 npm test  ← 2 workers
CUCUMBER_WORKERS=8 npm test  ← 8 workers (for high-end systems)
```

| Value | Mode | Speed | Best For |
|-------|------|-------|----------|
| `0` | Serial | 1x | Debugging |
| `2` | Parallel | 2x | Moderate systems |
| `4` | Parallel | 3-4x | Most systems (default) |
| `8` | Parallel | 4x | High-end systems only |

